<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="sec" style="background:#FFFFFF">
<div class="in">
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:48px 72px;align-items:flex-start">
<div class="stack" style="flex:1 1 300px;min-width:0;gap:20px;max-width:380px" data-reveal>
<h2 class="h2" data-split>Logistics scheduling, answered</h2>
<p class="txt">Curious how it works for your sites? We'll show Workofo with your own volumes and rules.</p>
</div>
<div class="retail-faq" data-lg-faq style="flex:2 1 520px;min-width:0" data-reveal>
<details><summary>What is logistics scheduling software?</summary><p>Logistics scheduling software builds shift plans around expected volumes instead of fixed patterns. Workofo forecasts pallets, orders and shipments, plans staff per location, zone and shift, and applies local labor rules.</p></details>
<details><summary>How does Workofo forecast warehouse workload?</summary><p>It uses incoming pallets, orders and shipment volumes to anticipate peaks and quiet periods across the day.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can Workofo assign people by skill and safety rules?</summary><p>Yes. Workers are assigned to activities based on competence and safety requirements, and differences in speed and experience are taken into account.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can we share staff between warehouses?</summary><p>Yes. You can reallocate, borrow or lend employee hours between locations. It works especially well for shared pools of 50–300 employees.</p></details>
<details><summary>How does Workofo handle absences and spikes?</summary><p>It suggests daily schedule adjustments so supervisors can cover unexpected absences and demand spikes quickly.</p></details>
<div class="retail-faq__more" data-lg-faq-more hidden>
<details><summary>Does Workofo support task-based staffing?</summary><p>Yes. Staffing can be planned per task and activity, not just per shift.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does Workofo follow local labor rules?</summary><p>Yes. Contracts, rest rules and local agreements are applied to every shift plan.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do supervisors keep control?</summary><p>Yes. Workofo suggests the plan; supervisors and operations managers review, adjust and publish it, and can test business rules over time.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is there an app for warehouse staff?</summary><p>Yes. Staff see their shifts, update availability and swap shifts in the Workofo mobile app.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is Workofo suitable for large logistics networks?</summary><p>Yes. Every site and zone is planned in one system, from a single warehouse to networks with thousands of employees.</p></details>
</div>
<button type="button" class="pill retail-faq-more__toggle" data-lg-faq-toggle aria-expanded="false">
<span class="retail-faq-more__more">Load more questions</span>
<span class="retail-faq-more__less">Show less</span>
<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
</button>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<BottomDemoCta
  demoHref={demoHref}
  headingId="lg-cta-heading"
  title="Book a demo built around your warehouse."
  sub="Bring your volumes, zones and shift rules, and we'll show you the plan Workofo would build."
  note="Most requests get a reply within one working day."
  tailoredSub="Your volumes, zones and rules"
  ariaLabel="Notifications: request received, demo tailored to your warehouse, demo booked."
/>

<script is:inline>
(function () {
  const faq = document.querySelector('[data-lg-faq]');
  if (!faq) return;
  const more = faq.querySelector('[data-lg-faq-more]');
  const btn = faq.querySelector('[data-lg-faq-toggle]');
  if (!more || !btn) return;
  const items = Array.from(more.querySelectorAll('details'));
  function setExpanded(on) {
    faq.classList.toggle('is-expanded', on);
    btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', on ? 'true' : 'false');
    if (on) {
      more.hidden = false;
      items.forEach(function (el, idx) {
        el.setAttribute('data-reveal', '');
        el.classList.remove('is-in');
        window.setTimeout(function () {
          el.classList.add('is-in');
        }, 40 + idx * 70);
      });
    } else {
      more.hidden = true;
      items.forEach(function (el) {
        el.classList.remove('is-in');
        el.removeAttribute('data-reveal');
      });
    }
  }
  btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
    setExpanded(!faq.classList.contains('is-expanded'));
  });
})();
</script>
